	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  error after restoring a db]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=12829#p12829"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>This is a french web forums about PostgreSQL. There are better options for english help, for example PostgreSQL Mailing lists.</p><p>Anyway, on your issue, it seems you&#039;re trying to restore your dump in the old database. The first error message, and a lot of others are like this : ERROR:&#160; constraint &quot;infodht_invhwtype_fk&quot; for relation &quot;infodht&quot; already exists ... it cannot restore your object because it already exists. You have to make sure that the database is empty (or at the very least, doesn&#039;t already contain objets of the same name).</p>]]></content>
